{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deliver","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"destinations","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},{"text":"..., ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchBufferLimit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":" = 100, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bufferDropReporter","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"BufferDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations16BufferDropReportV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"Continuation","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS12ContinuationV"},{"text":"? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsynchronousUnitOfWork","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsynchronousUnitOfWorkP"},{"text":"<()>\n","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"destinations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where each batch goes."}]}]},{"name":"batchBufferLimit","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"How many batches each destination may have waiting while it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"still receiving an earlier one. A tenth of how many dropped batches it keeps track of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to read back.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bufferDropReporter","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Where a report of each batch a destination’s full buffer drops is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yielded, as it is dropped; none by default. The delivery never finishes it, so one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reporter can serve the deliveries that replace one another.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A unit of work that completes once the last batch is delivered, and throws what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence throws, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when cancelled.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination(), vendor)","try await delivery.execute()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a slow destination delays only itself. When a batch arrives while a destination’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer already holds "},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" batches, the oldest waiting batch is dropped,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"logged and reported on "},{"code":"bufferDropReporter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":". Its records kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"memory only are lost. Those a store keeps are not: once that destination has received"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every batch waiting in its buffer, the delivery reads them back from the store and hands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them to that destination alone, one dropped batch at a time, oldest first. Read back, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record is as it was dropped: its "},{"code":"EventRecord.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values and context, which the delivery keeps meanwhile. The delivery keeps track of at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most ten times "},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dropped batches per destination; past that it forgets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the oldest, whose records stay in the store for the next launch, and logs it. Once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence ends, the work completes after every destination has received its last batch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ones read back included."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store keeps (those with an "},{"code":"EventRecord.deliveryTag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are reported to it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before a batch goes to any destination, and again once every destination’s "},{"code":"receive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has returned for it without being cancelled, when the store may forget them. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store couldn’t mark as being delivered is left out of the batch, and a batch left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no records isn’t sent. A record that some destination never received, because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store no longer kept it or couldn’t read it back when the delivery asked, is never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"acknowledged, so a store that still keeps it delivers it on the next launch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records the delivery has read but not delivered are lost to this run when it is cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or fails. Without a store they are gone; a store never had them acknowledged, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivers them on the next launch (unless its bound drops them first, which it reports)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing runs until the work is executed, and each execution reads the sequence again, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a delivery that finished or failed can be executed again (a retry). Cancelling it drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batches its destinations had waiting, and is permanent, as for every Afluent unit of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work: executing a cancelled delivery again throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" at once, so build a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new one instead."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batchBufferLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The work of delivering each batch of this sequence to every destination, until the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence ends."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Delivering","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"],"generated":true,"title":"Delivering"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/_concurrency\/asyncsequence\/deliver(to:batchbufferlimit:bufferdropreporter:)"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)","modules":[{"name":"Destinations","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"symbolKind":"method","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"[EventRecord]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"externalID":"s:Sci12Destinationss8SendableRzSay6Events11EventRecordVG7ElementRtzrlE7deliver2to16batchBufferLimit18bufferDropReporterQrAA11Destination_pd_SiScS12ContinuationVyAA0jM6ReportV_GSgtF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Deliver.swift#L59","fileName":"Deliver.swift"},"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","fragments":[{"te